Bugfix: Let shift+tab out of a header menu reach its toggle

Opening the app menu or the user menu moved the focus into the menu, but going
back from its first entry did not return to the toggle. It landed on the
search box at the other end of the header instead, because the menu sits after
the whole header in the document while it opens directly below its toggle on
screen.

Shift+tab on the first entry now moves the focus to the toggle it belongs to.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.3
